.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_MAP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_flat_map ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_filter ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_inspect ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_inspect_batch ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_inspect_core ,
.Nm dtfl_emit_record ,
.Nm dtfl_emit_reserve
.Nd per-record stream operators
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_flat_map "dtfl_stream *st" "const dtfl_type *out_type" "dtfl_map_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_filter "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_pred_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_inspect_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect_batch "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_inspect_batch_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect_core "dtfl_stream *st" "dtfl_inspect_core_fn fn" "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_emit_record "dtfl_emit *e" "const void *rec" "size_t len"
.Ft void *
.Fn dtfl_emit_reserve "dtfl_emit *e" "size_t len"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These operators transform or observe a stream record by record, each
producing a new stream in the same scope.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_flat_map
applies
.Fa fn
to every record of
.Fa st ,
at the record's time.
The callback emits zero or more records of
.Fa out_type
through the
.Vt dtfl_emit
sink, so it serves both map
.Pq one output per input
and flat map
.Pq any number .
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_filter
keeps the records of
.Fa st
for which
.Fa fn
returns true and drops the rest, preserving the record type.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect
calls
.Fa fn
once per record with its time, passing every record through unchanged.
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect_batch
calls
.Fa fn
once per message with its time and records.
.Fn dtfl_stream_inspect_core
also reports each frontier change, with
.Fa msg
set to
.Dv NULL
and the new frontier given as
.Fa frontier
and
.Fa nfrontier ;
a frontier is reported only when it changes.
All three pass records through unchanged.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_emit_record
appends a record of
.Fa len
bytes to the sink
.Fa e
passed to a producing callback.
.Fn dtfl_emit_reserve
instead reserves
.Fa len
bytes and returns where to write them, committing the record once
written; the returned pointer is valid until the next emit on
.Fa e .
.Pp
The context in
.Fa ctx
is passed to the callback as its first argument.
When
.Fa ctx
carries a destructor
.Pq Dv DTFL_CTX ,
the operator owns the context and releases it when the operator is
dropped.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_flat_map ,
.Fn dtfl_stream_filter
and the inspect functions return the new stream, owned by the scope.
.Fn dtfl_emit_reserve
returns a pointer to the reserved record bytes.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void add_one(void *ctx, const uint64_t *t, const void *rec,
    size_t len, dtfl_emit *out) {
	unsigned char buf[8];
	dtfl_put_u64(buf, dtfl_get_u64(rec) + 1);
	dtfl_emit_record(out, buf, sizeof buf);
}

static bool is_even(void *ctx, const void *rec, size_t len) {
	return dtfl_get_u64(rec) % 2 == 0;
}

dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_stream_flat_map(in, dtfl_type_u64(), add_one,
    DTFL_NOCTX);
s = dtfl_stream_filter(s, is_even, DTFL_NOCTX);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
A record type mismatch or an invalid stream is a programming error and
calls the panic hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_concat 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_to_stream 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn map ,
.Fn flat_map ,
.Fn filter ,
.Fn inspect ,
.Fn inspect_batch
and
.Fn inspect_core
operators.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
Each operator and its stream belong to the worker thread that built
them.
The callbacks run on that thread during the worker's steps and must not
be called directly.
